Z||000020||kempo||11-15-2001||08:20 PM||||This is a true show-quality fiero!  I love all the work you have done, it looks very sweet and professional.  What was all involved in mounting the actual dvd player in that location?  Also, I noticed the switches in your drivers ash tray compartment, what do they do?  Keep this fiero beautiful!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000021||edbone||11-15-2001||09:28 PM||||Ok to answer some of the questions,The start button is actually out of the new Honda I think its the h or s 2000 2 seater that just came out. I had to take the switch appart and with a meter find out which 2 of the 7 pins on the switch made contact and wired a relay of off of it to power the starter wire under the column. It is fully functionable.The dvd player is a Mobile car dvd called Farenheit by Power Accoustic.For this to work I had to untape and move the factory harness under the console and pound down some of the metal underneath to get the Dvd loading mechanism were you see it. I literally took the dvd appart and extended any wires and ribbon cables to get the rest of the dvd in the storage between the seats.Sounds easier than it was. Imagine taking a full size dvd and shrinking to fit there.The panell where the tv is in is a piece of MDF wood cut and shaped by hand to fit. The stereo consist of a pair of Mb quart 5.25 components in the front, Mb quart 4x6 in the rear, A Cadence 8 inch 300 watt woofer and a Mtx thunder amp to power the sub. The highs are powered of the new pontiac delco. Sound for the dvd is ran through a Fm modulator in stereo surround sound.The three switches in the ash tray are to power up the DVD,monitor, and fm Modulator.I think thats it. Exuse any misspelled words, Thanks for the interest. Any more questions, Ill be glad to answer. Eddie||||reg||1
